Now abstract away the cards

Across substrates, I think the Meta-Meta Engine is going to repeatedly find at least these operators:

Discovery advantage — being early to a strong strategy.

Diffusion tax — advantage decreases as knowledge spreads.

Concentration pressure — successful strategies attract population.

Counter-value — prevalence makes specialized counters increasingly profitable.

Expectation exploitation — once everyone expects X, deliberately choosing not-X can gain value.

Regulatory reset — whoever controls the rules can destroy an equilibrium without defeating it within its own rules.

Narrative displacement — cultural prestige and functional utility can diverge wildly.

Meta memory — supposedly obsolete strategies can become useful again when environmental conditions recur.

Meta leakage — a Silly Goose error: assuming something valuable in Meta A retains that value in Meta B.

And then the really important one:

Meta hunting becomes its own meta

You eventually stop trying to identify today’s winner and start looking for:

what is winning
→ why people discovered it
→ how quickly others will copy it
→ what copying it changes
→ what will beat the copied version
→ what intervention that produces
→ what becomes valuable afterward

That’s a trajectory, not a leaderboard.

So instead of predicting the next dominant Pokémon deck, stock strategy, military doctrine, fashion style, social-media format, or AI architecture independently, Pantheon can compare their meta-transition shapes.

If one domain currently looks structurally like:

early discovery → rapid diffusion → extreme concentration → counter-tech proliferation

and we have 200 historical examples across other substrates of what generally follows that state, those become priors for what to inspect next.

That’s the larger prize here:

Build a phylogeny of metas, then predict systems from where they are in the meta lifecycle rather than from what substrate they happen to inhabit.

That is substantially more powerful than studying any individual game.